{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is RVshare?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"RVshare is the top-rated and largest peer-to-peer RV rental marketplace in North America, connecting travelers with more than 100,000 RV rentals across the U.S. Travelers can rent everything from travel trailers and camper vans to luxury motorhomes directly from local RV owners, with optional delivery, secure online booking, and built-in protection coverage. RVshare also includes 24/7 roadside assistance and identity verification on every booking."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does RV rental work?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"RVshare lets travelers search RV rentals by destination, travel dates, RV type, amenities, and delivery options. Once booked, renters coordinate pickup or delivery directly with the RV owner through the RVshare platform. Every booking includes secure payment processing, identity verification, and roadside assistance, with optional insurance and trip protection plans available during checkout."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can I have an RV delivered?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Many RV owners on RVshare offer delivery directly to campgrounds, festivals, sporting events, and private properties. Delivery availability, distance limits, setup options, and fees are listed on each RV's detail page. Delivered RV rentals are especially popular among first-time RV travelers who prefer a ready-to-go experience without having to tow or drive the RV themselves."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I need a special license to drive an RV?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"In most cases, no special license is required to rent and drive an RV through RVshare. Most camper vans, travel trailers, and motorhomes can be operated with a standard driver's license. However, license requirements can vary based on RV size, vehicle weight, and state regulations, so renters should review local laws before traveling."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What protection is included with an RVshare rental?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"RVshare offers insurance and protection packages that can include liability coverage, collision and comprehensive protection, roadside assistance, and campsite liability coverage. Every booking also includes identity verification and fraud screening designed to help protect both RV owners and renters. Coverage options may vary by RV and reservation details."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why rent an RV through RVshare instead of a traditional RV rental company?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"RVshare gives travelers access to one of the largest selections of privately owned RV rentals in the U.S., including camper vans, travel trailers, toy haulers, and luxury motorhomes. Unlike traditional fleet rental companies, RVshare allows travelers to compare unique RV styles, delivery options, amenities, pet-friendly rentals, and local pickup locations directly from individual RV owners."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are first-time RV renters allowed on RVshare?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. RVshare is designed for both experienced RV travelers and first-time renters. RV owners provide walkthroughs, setup instructions, and delivery options that make RV travel more approachable for beginners. RVshare also offers roadside assistance and protection options to help travelers feel more confident before and during their trip."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What types of RVs can I rent on RVshare?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"RVshare offers a wide variety of RV rentals, including: Class A motorhomes, Class B camper vans, Class C motorhomes, Travel trailers, Fifth wheels, Toy haulers, Pop-up campers Availability varies by destination and travel dates."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does RVshare offer roadside assistance?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Every RVshare booking includes 24/7 emergency roadside assistance. Services may include towing, tire assistance, battery support, lockout service, fuel delivery, and RV technical support while traveling."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How does RVshare verify renters and owners?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"RVshare uses identity verification and fraud prevention systems designed to help create a safer rental experience for both RV owners and travelers. Verification may include government-issued ID checks, driver's license validation, and biometric identity confirmation before booking access is approved."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does an RV rental cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Most RV rentals range from about $100 to $300 per night and depend on several factors, including location, seasonality, RV type, amenities, and more."}}]}
"]

