{
	"@context": "https://schema.org",
	"@type": "FAQPage",
	"mainEntity": [

		{
			"@type": "Question",
			"name": "Does Orlando have live music, concerts and performing arts?",
			"acceptedAnswer": {
				"@type": "Answer",
				"text": "Absolutely. Orlando&#x2019;s live entertainment scene includes Broadway productions, concerts, comedy shows, symphony performances and intimate live music venues throughout the destination. Highlights include the Dr. Phillips Center for the Performing Arts (including Steinmetz Hall, Judson&#x2019;s Live and other theaters), Kia Center, House of Blues, Hard Rock Cafe, Timucua Arts Foundation, Blue Man Group, and many other options. Orlando also hosts major music festivals, including EDC Orlando and Vans Warped Tour, plus year-round concerts featuring local, national and international artists. <a href='https://www.visitorlando.com/events/all/?bounds=false&amp;view=grid&amp;sort=date&amp;filter_categories%5B0%5D=22&amp;filter_categories%5B1%5D=9'>Find live entertainment during your visit on our events calendar</a>."

			}
		},

		{
			"@type": "Question",
			"name": "Does Orlando have museums and galleries?",
			"acceptedAnswer": {
				"@type": "Answer",
				"text": "Certainly. Orlando offers a diverse collection of museums, galleries and cultural attractions for all interests. Explore inspiring collections at the Orlando Museum of Art and Rollins Museum of Art, discover local history at the Orange County Regional History Center, or experience rotating exhibitions, public art and galleries throughout Orlando&#x2019;s vibrant neighborhoods. <a href='https://www.visitorlando.com/blog/post/orlando-museums-galleries/'>Explore our best galleries and museums</a>."

			}
		},

		{
			"@type": "Question",
			"name": "Does Orlando have walkable neighborhoods?",
			"acceptedAnswer": {
				"@type": "Answer",
				"text": "Yes. Beyond the theme parks, Orlando is home to distinctive walkable neighborhoods filled with local restaurants, boutiques, entertainment and cultural experiences. Popular areas include Winter Park, Audubon Park Garden District, Ivanhoe Village, Mills 50&#xAE; and downtown Orlando&#x2019;s City District, where you can explore on foot while discovering local businesses and hidden gems. <a href='https://www.visitorlando.com/things-to-do/beyond-theme-parks/neighborhoods/'>Explore Orlando&#x2019;s neighborhoods and other Orange County communities you will want to visit</a>."

			}
		},

		{
			"@type": "Question",
			"name": "Does Orlando have live sports?",
			"acceptedAnswer": {
				"@type": "Answer",
				"text": "Orlando is home to several professional sports teams, including Orlando City Soccer Club (MLS) and Orlando Pride (NWSL) at Inter.co Stadium and the Orlando Magic (NBA) and Orlando Solar Bears (ECHL) at the Kia Center, with both venues located in downtown&#x2019;s Parramore District. In the adjacent West Lakes Market Street District, Camping World Stadium hosts college bowl games and other high-profile events. You can also enjoy college athletics with the UCF Knights, plus golf tournaments, tennis events and sporting competitions throughout the year, making it easy to cheer on your favorites or discover a new favorite team while you are here. <a href='https://www.visitorlando.com/things-to-do/beyond-theme-parks/sports/'>Learn more about Orlando&#x2019;s live sports offerings</a>."

			}
		},

		{
			"@type": "Question",
			"name": "Does Orlando have good golf courses?",
			"acceptedAnswer": {
				"@type": "Answer",
				"text": "Orlando is one of the world&#x2019;s premier golf destinations, with more than 100 golf courses designed by legendary architects and professional golfers. Popular options include Arnold Palmer&#x2019;s Bay Hill Club &amp; Lodge, Orange County National, Shingle Creek Golf Club, Waldorf Astoria Golf Club and The Ritz-Carlton Golf Club, Orlando. Whether you are a beginner or experienced player, you will find courses for every skill level. <a href='https://www.visitorlando.com/things-to-do/beyond-theme-parks/sports/golf/'>Explore opportunities to play and watch golf in Orlando</a>."

			}
		},

		{
			"@type": "Question",
			"name": "Does Orlando have outdoor activities?",
			"acceptedAnswer": {
				"@type": "Answer",
				"text": "Definitely. Orlando offers outdoor adventures ranging from kayaking, paddleboarding and fishing to airboat tours, nature trails and ecotourism experiences. You can explore scenic parks, natural springs, lakes and wildlife habitats, or enjoy outdoor recreation at attractions and resorts throughout the destination. <a href='https://www.visitorlando.com/things-to-do/beyond-theme-parks/nature-outdoors/'>Dive into Orlando&#x2019;s natural wonders</a>."

			}
		},

		{
			"@type": "Question",
			"name": "Does Orlando have good places to eat?",
